      "writtenOn": "2026-05-19T16:53:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I re-investigated this a bit more, and I think my initial understanding of the issue was incorrect, so I reverted this, and updated the tests. The issue was that because the tests are modifying the injected commands but still initially issuing them through the wire-client, there is a desync on the actual ids in the bookkeeping in the client. I think the correct behavior is to actually fail on the server-side when we try to `FlushClient` in the tests, so I updated them all and added a comment to document it.\n\nI think the takeaway is that trying to test with both a real client while modifying the command buffer makes things really weird... But I guess that\u0027s just the reality of these tests lol.",
      "parentUuid": "b95d6985_8cb6c4cb",
      "revId": "e632cedb5a391d732ea4912641095492f46c0daf",
